    {
      "component_id": "c_018",
      "class": "android.support.v7.widget.n",
      "text": "Search Select a dictionary and type a word in the Search field. Dictionaries Additional dictionaries can be downloaded by clicking on the Add (+) button. Downloaded dictionaries will stay on the device and can be viewed offline. Dictionaries can be removed by clicking Add (+) and on the dictionary in the displayed list. It is possible to evaluate and give a note to a dictionary. Click Add, then long click on the dictionary and click on Note. Bookmarks / History Slide the left border (or click the upper left icon) to open history and bookmarks. Advanced search / Crossword search Wildcard characters can be used to perform advanced searches. \u2022 Use ? to replace a single letter. For example, searching ?at will give: bat, cat, fat, hat\u2026 \u2022 Use * to replace from 0 to N letters. For example, searching m*e will give: machine, made, magazine, me, message\u2026 \u2022 Wildcards can be combined: \u2022 m?t*e will give: mate, mute, materialize\u2026 \u2022 use *cat* to find words containing cat \u2022 Wildcards can be used many times. e?ecu???? will give: executing, executive\u2026 It can be useful to solve crossword puzzles. Text to speech A text to speech feature can be activated by pressing Menu and then Text to speech. It is able to read the current definition. If only a part of the text is selected, only this part will be read. It is also possible to read from current cursor position. Cursor position can be changed by clicking where you want on the text. The more appropriate language will be selected automatically. Text to speech availability and installed languages depend on your device.",
